<article class="env-lemma" id="00LL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00LL">Lemma <span data-tag="00LL">10.63.18</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$. Let $I \subset \mathfrak m$ be an ideal. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module. The following are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
There exists an $x \in I$ which is not a zerodivisor on $M$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We have $I \not\subset \mathfrak q$ for all $\mathfrak q \in \text{Ass}(M)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If there exists a nonzerodivisor $x$ in $I$, then $x$ clearly cannot be in any associated prime of $M$. Conversely, suppose $I \not\subset \mathfrak q$ for all $\mathfrak q \in \text{Ass}(M)$. In this case we can choose $x \in I$, $x \not\in \mathfrak q$ for all $\mathfrak q \in \text{Ass}(M)$ by Lemmas <a href="/tag/00LC" data-tag="00LC">10.63.5</a> and <a href="/tag/00DS" data-tag="00DS">10.15.2</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00LD" data-tag="00LD">10.63.9</a> the element $x$ is not a zerodivisor on $M$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>